# [[one hundred thousand|One hundred thousand]] (10⁵): {{l|mul|100,000}}, that is, with [[Indian#Adjective|Indian]] [[digit#Noun|digit]] [[grouping#Noun|grouping]], 1,00,000.
#: {{alti|en|lac<qq:dated>}}
#: {{hol|en|crore}}
#* {{RQ:Purchas Pilgrimage|chapter=Of the Great Mogor|page=406|passage=They ſay the VVorld ſhall laſt foure Ages; or VVorlds, vvhereof three are paſt. The firſt laſted ſeuenteene '''''Laches''''' (euery '''''Laches''''' containeth a hundred thouſand yeares) and 28000 yeares. Men in that VVorld liued tenne thouſand yeares, vvere of great ſtature of bodie, and great ſinceritie of minde.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:James Talboys Wheeler|J[ames] Talboys Wheeler]], compiler|chapter=Governorship of Mr. {{w|Nathaniel Higginson}}. 1692–1698.|title=Madras in the Olden Time: Being a History of the Presidency from the First Foundation of the Governorship of {{w|Thomas Pitt}}, Grandfather of the Earl of Chatham. 1639–1702.{{nb...|Compiled from Official Records.}}|location=Madras|publisher={{...|Printed for}} [[w:Higginbotham's|J[oshua] Higginbotham]],{{nb...|Mount Road}}, by Graves and Co., Scottish Press|year='''1693''' January 2 (date written; Gregorian calendar)|year_published=1861|page=262|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/madrasinoldentim01whee/page/262/mode/1up|oclc=969787585|passage=[T]he Mahrattas having offered Alimerdy Khan his liberty for a '''lak''' of Pagodas {{quote-gloss|a unit of currency}}; he does in the Nabob's name desire that the Governor of Madras would receive jewels and money to that amount into his custody, {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:Patrick O'Brian|Patrick O’Brian]]|title=[[w:Post Captain (novel)|Post Captain]]|location=London|publisher=[[w:HarperCollins|HarperCollinsPublishers]]|year=1972|year_published=1998|page=18|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/postcaptain0000obri_a5m1/page/18/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-00-221657-9|passage=[S]he had gone out to India to keep house for her expensive, raffish father, and she had lived there in splendid style even after her marriage to a penniless young man, her father's aide-de-camp, {{...}} But they were both killed in the same engagement against [[w:Tipu Sultan|Tippoo Sahib]], her father owing ten '''lakhs''' of rupees and her husband nearly half that sum.}}
#* {{quote-journal |en |date=2025-09-08 |last=Vijayakumar |first=Sanjay |title=Tamil Nadu second biggest market for small business credit: study |journal=w:The Hindu |url=https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/tamil-nadu/tamil-nadu-second-biggest-market-for-small-business-credit-study/article70022367.ece |passage=Tamil Nadu is the second biggest market for small business credit, accounting for 9.3% of the national total, as per a joint report by Small Industries Development Bank of India (SIDBI) and credit bureau CRIF High Mark. As of June 30, 2025, Tamil Nadu had an outstanding small business credit portfolio of about ₹4.21 '''lakh''' crore, up 15.7% from ₹3.64 '''lakh''' crore as of June 30 2024, the report said. Maharashtra remained the largest market with ₹6.0 '''lakh''' crore in outstanding credit, while Tamil Nadu, Gujarat (₹3.69 '''lakh''' crore), Uttar Pradesh (₹3.61 '''lakh''' crore), and Karnataka (₹3.18 '''lakh''' crore) round out the top five by portfolio size. Uttar Pradesh registered highest outstanding portfolio growth of 20.7% on a year-on-year basis. The report defines "Small Business" as those businesses that have an aggregated credit exposure not exceeding ₹5 crore from the formal lending system.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250911015512/https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/tamil-nadu/tamil-nadu-second-biggest-market-for-small-business-credit-study/article70022367.ece}}
#* {{quote-journal |en |date=2025-09-08 |last=Khan |first=Haider Ali |title=GST simplification will do good for sellers and buyers, says Amazon Country Manager |journal=w:The Hindu |url=https://www.thehindu.com/sci-tech/technology/gst-simplification-will-do-good-for-sellers-and-buyers-says-amazon-country-manager/article70025724.ece |passage=GST {{quote-gloss|Goods and Services Tax}} simplification will do good for sellers and buyers, said Samir Kumar, Country Manager, Amazon India {{...}} Amazon said it is updating its systems with the revised GST codes for sellers to move to the new tax structure {{...}} Amazon said it has over 17 '''lakh''' sellers on its platform and around 2,000 last mile delivery stations across the country.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250915084314/https://www.thehindu.com/sci-tech/technology/gst-simplification-will-do-good-for-sellers-and-buyers-says-amazon-country-manager/article70025724.ece}}

